# CVE-2024-23342 — python-ecdsa "Minerva" timing side-channel attack.
# Upstream (python-ecdsa) has stated they will not fix this: it requires
# constant-time arithmetic that the pure-Python implementation doesn't
# provide. Pulled in transitively via python-jose[cryptography]. No fixed
# version exists to upgrade to, so this is accepted as a known risk.
CVE-2024-23342

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack 1.1.2) and CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools 70.3.0)
# — Trivy flags these under an aggregate "Python" target sourced from a
# third-party SBOM embedded in a compiled dependency wheel (see Trivy's own
# "Third-party SBOM may lead to inaccurate vulnerability detection" warning
# in the scan log). That SBOM describes the *build-time* toolchain used by
# PyPI's infrastructure when the wheel was originally compiled upstream —
# not what's actually installed here. The real filesystem scan in the same
# report confirms the versions actually installed are clean:
# msgpack-1.2.1.dist-info and setuptools-84.0.0.dist-info both show 0
# vulnerabilities. Ignored as a confirmed false positive.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
